WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:02.990
Slough, the mid-1990s.

2
00:00:03.040 --> 00:00:07.130
A local charity records gang violence
among young people from the Hindu,

3
00:00:07.180 --> 00:00:10.850
Muslim and Sikh communities
of Slough and Southall.

4
00:00:10.900 --> 00:00:14.680
In 1998, Channel 4
screened The Peacemaker.

5
00:00:14.730 --> 00:00:19.710
Conflict-resolution expert Dr Dudley
Weeks mediated between the gangs.

6
00:00:19.760 --> 00:00:21.750
Weeks backed a group led by young people,

7
00:00:21.800 --> 00:00:23.430
for young people.

8
00:00:23.480 --> 00:00:26.950
It became Aik Saath: Together As One.

9
00:00:27.000 --> 00:00:30.030
Decades on, how would
you judge if it worked?

10
00:00:30.080 --> 00:00:31.010
Fewer fights?

11
00:00:31.060 --> 00:00:32.890
How young people feel?

12
00:00:32.940 --> 00:00:34.030
Something wider?

13
00:00:34.080 --> 00:00:37.530
In this mission, you'll test
Slough's change with population,

14
00:00:37.580 --> 00:00:41.290
pay, deprivation, health
and air quality data.

15
00:00:41.340 --> 00:00:45.230
Then you'll set the charity's work beside
national and council strategies for

16
00:00:45.280 --> 00:00:46.290
the town.

17
00:00:46.340 --> 00:00:51.330
Your mission: decide how to judge whether
Slough's youth-led peace strategy worked.
